<title>USA: Wallace Computer authorizes share buyback.</title>
<headline>Wallace Computer authorizes share buyback.</headline>
<dateline>LISLE, Ill. 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wallace Computer Services Inc said Friday its board of directors authorized the repurchase of up to $100 milion of the company's stock.</p>
<p>Shares will be repurchased from time to time at prevailing market prices, the company said.  </p>
<p>The buyback follows a prior $100 million repurchase program which was completed in April 1997. Under the previous program, 3,444,200 shares were repurchased. As of April 30, Wallace had 43,033,506 shares outstanding.</p>
<p>Shares of Wallace, which provides information management supplies and services, closed 1/4 higher at 27-5/8.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
</text>
